[s0l0!-header][h1]Relational Operators[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

[b]Relational operators[/b] are used to compare two values and return a [b]bool[/b] as the result: [b]true[/b] when the comparison condition holds, and [b]false[/b] when it does not.

[s0l0!-header][b]Let's see them in action:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="go" codeId="3308"]x := 42
y := 8
    
// equal to
fmt.Println(x == y)
    
// not equal to
fmt.Println(x != y)
    
// greater than
fmt.Println(x > y)
    
// less than
fmt.Println(x < y) [/code]
[note]The [b]greater or equal to >=[/b] and [b]less or equal to <=[/b] operators are also available.[/note]

